					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12859918#post-4450371</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12859918/a-special-holiday-message-from-scp-999#post-4450371</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 20 Dec 2019 06:28:27 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Amelia Wright</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3754950</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I hate fun -1.</p> <p>In all seriousness, I want to say that I'm not downvoting because the song and piece are badly written; far from it. I respect the hell out of posting a <em>song</em> here, and I respect both the effort as well as the courage in making this tale happen. That being said, I don't really care for this kind of style in having jokey, song pieces like this. There was already one tale that had already did it just fine, and I think the concept only can go far enough with one. Also, I really don't like 999. No discrespect to the original author, but the little guy aged as well as milk, and I just don't like the character.</p> <p>TLDR: Not my thing, at all, but I commend the effort and passion.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
